<http://data.silknow.org/object/8421853c-5a64-3047-bfaa-598b934d956d>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Dress fabric of brocaded silk satin with silk and metal threads.\n\nSatin ground, twill binding.\nWarp: dark blue or black silk, indeterminable twist.\nWeft: silk, dark blue, dark green [largely decayed], bright red, all indeterminable twist.\nMetal thread: silver-gilt strip close Z-wound on deep yellow silk, indeterminable twist.\nDark blue or black ground with a small repeating pattern of leafy lozenges joined by a circular motif.  Each lozenge frames a stylised plant with red flowers and green leaves. The lozenge, the joining motifs and the plant details are worked in metal thread."@en , "Middle East, Textile; Dress fabric of brocaded silk satin with silk and metal threads, Iran, 1800-1899"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/764b6880-55c1-3518-9027-57b1b94c0721> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Dress fabric of brocaded silk satin with silk and metal threads.\n\nSatin ground, twill binding.\nWarp: dark blue or black silk, indeterminable twist.\nWeft: silk, dark blue, dark green [largely decayed], bright red, all indeterminable twist.\nMetal thread: silver-gilt strip close Z-wound on deep yellow silk, indeterminable twist.\nDark blue or black ground with a small repeating pattern of leafy lozenges joined by a circular motif.  Each lozenge frames a stylised plant with red flowers and green leaves. The lozenge, the joining motifs and the plant details are worked in metal thread."@en , "Middle East, Textile; Dress fabric of brocaded silk satin with silk and metal threads, Iran, 1800-1899"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/8421853c-5a64-3047-bfaa-598b934d956d/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/8421853c-5a64-3047-bfaa-598b934d956d/dimension/2> ;
        dc:identifier                  "T.21:68-1955" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs>
                <https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O153894> .

